{"files": [{"id": 47099656, "name": "ppat.1011970.g001.tif", "size": 544384, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/47099656", "supplied_md5": "23cad65ba7dd11af4e44eda6b6591793", "computed_md5": "23cad65ba7dd11af4e44eda6b6591793", "mimetype": "image/tiff"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 4308, "full_name": "Yan Chen", "first_name": "Yan", "last_name": "Chen", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Yan_Chen", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841048, "full_name": "Rodney P. Kincaid", "first_name": "Rodney P.", "last_name": "Kincaid", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841051, "full_name": "Kelley Bastin", "first_name": "Kelley", "last_name": "Bastin", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841054, "full_name": "Devin N. Fachko", "first_name": "Devin N.", "last_name": "Fachko", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841057, "full_name": "Rebecca L. Skalsky", "first_name": "Rebecca L.", "last_name": "Skalsky", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/Genome-wide_miRNA-focused_CRISPR_Cas9_screen_identifies_cellular_miR-142_as_a_regulator_of_EBV_reactivation_/26051923", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p>A. Schematic of the miRNA-focused CRISPR/Cas9 loss-of-function screen carried out in EBV-positive MutuI-iCas9 BL cells. B. DrugZ-calculated normZ score plotted versus miRNA gene rank. Red indicates targets that were significantly enriched in gp350-positive population while black indicates targets significantly enriched in the gp350-negative population (p-value < 0.05). Highlighted is miR-142 which showed the most significant changes. C. EBV lytic transcripts are upregulated in miR-142 mutant cells. Four EBV lytic genes were measured by qRT-PCR in MutuI-iCas9 cells transduced with either a control gRNA (Neg3) or the top two scoring guide-RNAs (gRNAs) against miR-142 (10024 or 10033). Cells were either mock or anti-IgM treated for 48 hrs. Values are normalized to GAPDH and shown relative to anti-IgM treated Neg3 control cells. Shown is the average of six independent experiments. By Student\u2019s t-test, *p<0.05. D. and E. miR-142-3p and miR-142-5p expression in multiple B cell lines. Total RNA was extracted from DLBCLs (IBL1, IBL4, BCKN1), LCLs (LCL16.1, 17.1, 17.2), EBV-positive BL (KemI, RaeI, Raji, MutuI, Akata), EBV-positive BL treated with anti-Ig for 24 hr (MutuI, Akata) and EBV-negative BL (BJAB, BL41, Ramos). miRNAs were assessed by Taqman qRT-PCR. Values are normalized to miR-16 and reported relative to IBL1.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 544384, "created_date": "2024-06-17T17:37:25Z", "modified_date": "2024-06-28T17:35:36Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["b cell receptor", "surface ig cross", "xlink \"> reactivation", "142 targets related", "142 enhanced levels", "restricts ebv entry", "support viral infection", "infected bl cells", "cells using anti", "ebv lytic phase", "erk signaling initiated", "ebv reactivation", "mapk signaling", "lytic stage", "ig antibodies", "induce reactivation", "ebv latency", "taken together", "significant role", "results show", "latency plays", "key regulator", "immediate early", "grna library", "genetic ablation", "gain insight", "fully understood", "effects could", "dabrafenib ).", "clip experiments", "burkitt lymphoma", "based screen", "barr virus"], "keywords": ["b cell receptor", "surface ig cross", "xlink \"> reactivation", "142 targets related", "142 enhanced levels", "restricts ebv entry", "support viral infection", "infected bl cells", "cells using anti", "ebv lytic phase", "erk signaling initiated", "ebv reactivat